R3 runtime binaries: reproducible clean replacements

These files replace the same paths in the pinned HiBy R3 Pro II and R3 II
2025 base images. The replacements remove build-directory strings while
preserving their runtime ELF interface. Firmware packaging verifies each
SHA-256 against firmware/r3-runtime.sha256 and applies this tree only to R3
boards.

Seven files are the canonical clean rebuilds recorded by
firmware/r1_base_v2.json under base_layer_clean_rebuilds.files. Their source
versions, configure options, patches, Ingenic GCC 5.2 toolchain, and
-fdebug-prefix-map handling are documented by that build record and the
scripts/build/base recipes. Their pre- and post-build hashes are listed in
firmware/r3-runtime.sha256's companion provenance in the repository.

usr/bin/gatttool is BlueZ 5.87's deprecated command-line tool. It was built
from the pinned upstream archive (SHA-256
26bdcf2cebd7310c6f598850606b037ef0c515fe6608ebc54d22c50c4c32b35f) using
scripts/build/base/bluetooth/build_base_bluez.sh. The build recipe targets
MIPS32r2 O32 hard-float and configures through a relative source path. The
staged binary is stripped with MIPS-target strip --strip-unneeded to remove
residual generic toolchain strings. The vendor version, source archive, and
final replacement hash are recorded in firmware/r3-runtime-provenance.json
and firmware/r3-runtime.sha256.

ABI comparison against both R3 board images found identical ELF class,
endianness, MIPS32r2 O32 hard-float flags, interpreter, dynamic dependencies,
SONAMEs where present, and versioned dynamic symbol tables for all eight
replacements. No replacement has RPATH or RUNPATH. This is static ABI evidence;
device runtime validation remains part of firmware release verification.

License texts for ALSA and BlueALSA are provided beside this notice. BlueZ
5.87's COPYING and COPYING.LIB are provided in /usr/share/licenses/bluez.
